meta {
  name: QR Check-in
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/physical/sessions/{{physicalSessionId}}/check-ins
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "type": "QR",
    "qrCredentials": "{{physicalQrCredentials}}",
    "deviceId": "{{physicalDeviceId}}",
    "deviceToken": "{{physicalDeviceSecret}}"
  }
}

docs {
  #38, US-PHYSICAL-001 escenario 2. Public at the filter level (`permitAll`)
  — the door reader authenticates against the device registry (#266) with
  `deviceId` (the registered device's UUID) and `deviceToken` (that device's
  own secret), verified inside the use case, never a Bearer token.
  `qrCredentials` comes from `POST /access-qr` (a Bearer-authenticated
  student endpoint, not in this folder).

  Prerequisite: run `devices/Register Device` first (ADMIN token). Its
  post-response script stores `physicalDeviceId` and `physicalDeviceSecret`,
  which this request reads; `devices/Rotate Device Secret` refreshes the
  secret. The raw secret is shown only once, so a device registered outside
  Bruno needs both variables set by hand.

  Validation order before touching Redis: device authentication, QR shape,
  sessionId match, signature, expiry, session existence/window, confirmed
  capacity assignment. Only a request that clears all of those reaches the
  locks.

  Success contract: 201 on the first valid scan, 200 on any idempotent
  replay of the same QR — the attendance row count never grows on replay.
  Error contract:
    400 INVALID_REQUEST / INVALID_QR_CREDENTIAL → malformed body or QR bound
        to a different session
    401 INVALID_DEVICE_TOKEN → unknown deviceId, deviceId that is not a UUID, or
        wrong deviceToken (all three look identical)
    401 DEVICE_REVOKED       → revoked device, correct secret
    401 DEVICE_EXPIRED       → device past its expiresAt, correct secret
    403 SESSION_CANCELLED | OUTSIDE_CHECK_IN_WINDOW | CAPACITY_ASSIGNMENT_REQUIRED
    404 SESSION_NOT_FOUND
    409 ALREADY_PROCESSING
    410 EXPIRED_QR_CREDENTIAL
    503 CHECK_IN_DEGRADED (Redis unavailable, fail-closed)
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
}
